      "content": "It's a perfectly natural feeling when the world moves on and you're left behind, a kind of obsolescence that stings. But what you've learned isn't just a set of skills; it's a massive, intricate structure of knowledge that is now just a very complex, very expensive piece of hardware. You can choose to let that hardware rust, or you can find the most efficient way to power it down, and the sheer weight of that accumulated experience can be a very powerful thing to use as a guide.",
